# 4.1.scenario.elimination.assay.enumerate.stone

## .what

for **each live scenario**, name the test(s) that could rule it out. the assay phase exists to shrink
the superposition — so first enumerate, per scenario, what observation or test would eliminate it.

## .inputs

- `3.3.scenario.disentangle.correlation.blend.yield.md` — the coarse-ranked live set + floor
- `1.3.intake.gaps.yield.md` — the knowledge gaps (some tests close these)

## .do

- for every live scenario (the low-probability / high-severity landmines too), name the test, exam
  sign, or observation that would **rule it out** (or confirm it)
- a scenario with **no** test to rule it out is a standing hazard — flag it plainly (it stays live)
- prefer tests that separate **between** scenarios (high information), not just confirm one

## .emit

into `4.1.scenario.elimination.assay.enumerate.yield.md` — a test-per-scenario map.

## .done when

every live scenario has a named test to rule it out (or a flag that none exists), with the
between-scenario tests marked.
